# EdCoach AI - Cursor Rules

## Project Context
AI-powered instructional coaching platform for K-12 schools using Next.js 15, Convex, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS.

## Key Patterns

### Design System Integration
- ALWAYS use design tokens from `lib/design-tokens.ts` instead of hardcoded values
- Use `cn()` utility for conditional classes
- Follow established component patterns in `components/ui/`

### TypeScript Standards
- Prefer TypeScript over JavaScript for all code
- Use proper type annotations and Convex generated types
- Follow strict TypeScript configuration

### Component Structure
```typescript
interface ComponentProps {
  className?: string;
  children?: React.ReactNode;
  // Feature-specific props
}

export function Component({ className, children, ...props }: ComponentProps) {
  return (
    <div className={cn("base-styles", className)} {...props}>
      {children}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Convex Backend Patterns
- Use proper function types: `query`, `mutation`, `action`, `internalMutation`
- Implement comprehensive validators for all functions
- Follow Convex best practices for performance and real-time features

### Next.js App Router
- Use proper route groups: `(dashboard)`, `(marketing)`, `(setup)`
- Implement loading.tsx and error.tsx for better UX
- Use Suspense boundaries for optimal loading experiences

